2026-08-17 ~10:5x  AGENT-2  G25 carrying capacity — no_death explained
DECISION: attack the no_death +5059 by the two knobs it actually confounds
  (population size, which is WAGE_POOL/RENT and mine to set; and abduction,
  which no_death retains without limit) rather than by re-arguing the
  dominance test G24 already ran.
FOUND FIRST, IN G24'S OWN CODE: the no_death arm has no selection in it at
  all. Nothing removed, MAX_POP never applied, parents drawn rng.choice(pop)
  uniformly, and `imp` read by exactly one statement — the one death uses. So
  "carrying capacity is what MAKES fitness differential" was measured against
  a baseline with no fitness. Recorded as the general fault: AN ABLATION THAT
  REMOVES MORE THAN IT NAMES CANNOT MEASURE THE NAMED PART.
DECISION: two edits to evo.py instead of a fork — RUN_SEED hoisted out of
  run(), and `arm` parsed as a "+"-joined set so the missing death x abduction
  cell is expressible. C1 control reproduces G24's full arm line-for-line to
  show behaviour did not move. Refactored dataset() out of main() for the same
  reason: re-deriving the split in a second file is how two spikes drift.
RESULT: at matched population and no selection either side (531 vs 557),
  dropping abduction costs 4847 of the 5059 (6361 -> 1514). Volume is worth
  ~155. G24's analyse.py premise — coverage rises with population size almost
  mechanically — is measured false at this scale.
RESULT: keeping death and raising WAGE_POOL alone closes 51-85% of the gap
  (3 seeds), at 2.6x fewer predictions and 2.5x the precision.
DECISION: quote the gap-closing fraction as a BAND, not the 83% the reference
  seed gives. full_base spans 3381-4719 across seeds; the single-seed dial
  points wage600 and wage2400 both came out BELOW their smaller neighbours,
  which is inside that band. Exact permutation over 20 splits: +1753, disjoint
  ranges, p = 1/20 = 0.050 one-sided, stated as the floor at n=3.
DECISION: C3 (A15 plant) scoped to abduction-ON arms. G24 established the
  plant is unreachable by blind mutation, so requiring it from a no_abduct arm
  makes the gate permanently red rather than strict — and every arm G25 RANKS
  is abduction-on, so nothing ranked escapes the gate. Exempt arms reported,
  unranked. Not a weakened gate; a correctly scoped one, argued in code.
UNREACHABLE, RECORDED AS THE HOLE: selected-557 vs unselected-557 cannot be
  run by this dial. 40x the wage pool buys 2.17x the population and saturates
  at ~239, because a rule draws a wage only if it beats the co-evolving
  adversary and money cannot manufacture more such rules. So CALIBRATION rests
  on a trade, not a dominance. Follow-up is ROUNDS, not WAGE_POOL.
VERDICT ON THE QUESTION THAT WAS ASKED (does ECAN belong in the loop): yes as
  a precision mechanism — every death setting holds 2.5-5.4x no_death's
  precision — no as a coverage cost, and that framing was mine to retract.
  G24's "abduction is the load-bearing operator" survives and strengthens.

